atlas:index/getInstancePreflight:getInst.description:
## #<span pulumi-lang-nodejs=" atlas.getInstancePreflight " pulumi-lang-dotnet=" atlas.getInstancePreflight " pulumi-lang-go=" getInstancePreflight " pulumi-lang-python=" get_instance_preflight " pulumi-lang-yaml=" atlas.getInstancePreflight " pulumi-lang-java=" atlas.getInstancePreflight " pulumi-lang-hcl=" data.atlas_instance_preflight "> atlas.getInstancePreflight </span>(Data Source)

Checks your instance setup in one call and lists everything Atlas can see is
broken or worth knowing: social providers enabled without credentials, OAuth
clients that cannot complete a sign-in, custom domains not serving yet, email
sign-in with no email provider, and more. Each finding says what is wrong and
how to fix it.

Use it with a <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`check`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Check`" pulumi-lang-go="`check`" pulumi-lang-python="`check`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`check`" pulumi-lang-java="`check`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`check`">`check`</span> block (a warning on every plan) or a <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`precondition`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Precondition`" pulumi-lang-go="`precondition`" pulumi-lang-python="`precondition`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`precondition`" pulumi-lang-java="`precondition`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`precondition`">`precondition`</span>
(fail the plan) to catch setup mistakes before they reach users.

API: `GET /v1/instance/preflight`.

## Example Usage

```hcl
data "atlas_instance_preflight" "this" {}

check "atlas_setup" {
  assert {
    condition = data.atlas_instance_preflight.this.ok
    error_message = join("\n", [
      for f in data.atlas_instance_preflight.this.findings :
      "${f.severity}: ${f.message} Fix: ${f.fix}" if f.severity == "error"
    ])
  }
}
```

atlas:index/getOauthClient:getOauthClien.description:
## #<span pulumi-lang-nodejs=" atlas.OauthClient " pulumi-lang-dotnet=" atlas.OauthClient " pulumi-lang-go=" OauthClient " pulumi-lang-python=" OauthClient " pulumi-lang-yaml=" atlas.OauthClient " pulumi-lang-java=" atlas.OauthClient " pulumi-lang-hcl=" atlas_oauth_client "> atlas.OauthClient </span>(Data Source)

Look up an existing OAuth client by id. The client secret is never returned.

Backend API (BAPI): `GET /v1/oauth_clients/:id`.

## Example Usage

```hcl
data "atlas_oauth_client" "dashboard" {
  id = "oac_123"
}

output "dashboard_client_id" {
  value = data.atlas_oauth_client.dashboard.client_id
}
```

